                <pb facs="1202" n="1184" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg1184"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">834.00/8–246: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Paraguay</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Beaulac</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-08-02">August 2, 1946</date>.<lb/>[Received August 2—1:44
                        p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>357. Council of Ministers yesterday approved (1) broad political amnesty (2)
                    right of workers to organize in principle (3) participation of Communist Party
                    in politics.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaulac</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
